WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.743
The activities in this course lead to
different technical deliverables.

2
00:00:03.823 --> 00:00:07.013
Attack surface work produces inventories
and exposure relationships.

3
00:00:07.093 --> 00:00:09.133
Vulnerability research explains a
weakness,

4
00:00:09.213 --> 00:00:12.927
while vulnerability management prioritizes
and tracks weaknesses across assets.

5
00:00:13.007 --> 00:00:16.197
Code review and application testing
investigate security properties;

6
00:00:16.277 --> 00:00:19.886
infrastructure assessment examines
effective configuration and permissions.

7
00:00:19.966 --> 00:00:22.582
Detection engineering produces tested
monitoring logic.

8
00:00:22.662 --> 00:00:26.271
Incident response and forensics
reconstruct activity from preserved evidence.

9
00:00:26.351 --> 00:00:29.123
Intelligence analysis evaluates sources
and relationships.

10
00:00:29.203 --> 00:00:32.132
AI-assisted threat modeling connects
assets, trust boundaries,

11
00:00:32.212 --> 00:00:34.827
plausible attack paths, and controls to
design decisions.

12
00:00:34.907 --> 00:00:38.621
AI-assisted risk management connects those
findings with business consequences,

13
00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:41.316
treatment options, accountable owners, and
review dates.

14
00:00:41.396 --> 00:00:43.226
Threat scenarios inform risk decisions,

15
00:00:43.306 --> 00:00:46.863
and business priorities help determine
which design gaps need attention first.

16
00:00:46.943 --> 00:00:50.657
Choose an activity connected to your
responsibilities or interests and study its AI

17
00:00:50.737 --> 00:00:51.940
applications more deeply.

18
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:55.733
Truth Surge's AI-focused learning paths
and specialized activity courses provide

19
00:00:55.813 --> 00:00:57.330
directions for that exploration.

20
00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:01.385
Operator-development subjects strengthen
reasoning, learning, and decision-making.

21
00:01:01.465 --> 00:01:05.231
The traditional cybersecurity reference
library supplies explanations when a task

22
00:01:05.311 --> 00:01:08.815
exposes a knowledge gap; it is not a
compulsory sequence of hundreds of courses.

23
00:01:08.895 --> 00:01:11.563
Assistance may reduce repetitive work,
organize evidence,

24
00:01:11.643 --> 00:01:13.526
or make broader investigation practical.

25
00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.646
Its value is established within the
activity,

26
00:01:15.726 --> 00:01:19.073
through a better-supported inventory,
finding, detection, threat model,

27
00:01:19.153 --> 00:01:19.938
or risk decision.

28
00:01:20.018 --> 00:01:23.365
Check generated claims against source
records, make uncertainty visible,

29
00:01:23.445 --> 00:01:26.113
and verify whether planned changes
achieved their purpose.

30
00:01:26.193 --> 00:01:30.011
Established technical expertise and
accountable human judgment remain the basis for

31
00:01:30.091 --> 00:01:32.340
deciding whether the result deserves
confidence.
